# Proposed features recognized from drilled_plate.step by sidecar/import_step.py
# (contract v1 -- see sidecar/CONTRACT.md). Review before use:
# recognition proposes, it does not machine.

# F1: outer profile under top cap F3: vertical wall loop F1 F2 F6 F4, top at z=15.0, base at z=0.0, material inside the loop (CHECKLIST row 2.2)
# consume with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F1_Profile, comp=control)  [the feature carries its own z + extent]
# the loop is wound CW: material inside, tool outside (the winding convention,
# DECISIONS.md -> "Row-2.4 side selector")
# comp=control is required on Contour runs: recognized boundaries carry rounded
# corners tessellated to chords, and engine comp hard-errors on rounded-corner
# offsets (DECISIONS.md -> "recognized contours propose comp=control")
feature F1_Profile ProfileBoss(z=15.0, extent=15.0
    0.0 0.0
    0.0 80.0
    100.0 80.0
    100.0 0.0
)

# F3: planar, normal +Z, topmost planar face (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
feature F3_Top Plane(z=15.0)

# F7: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; bottom opens through -- a drillable through hole (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# consume with: run Form(points=[F7_Hole], tool=..., cycle=Simple)  [the bore carries its own extent, measured down from the stock top]
# through hole -- drill past extent=15.0 by the tip's point length for full-diameter breakthrough
# or finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F7_Hole, stepover=...)
feature F7_Hole CylinderBore(dia=12.0, extent=15.0, x=20.0, y=20.0)

# F8: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; drill-point bottom F11 (included angle 118.072 deg) -- a drilled hole (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# consume with: run Form(points=[F8_Hole], tool=..., cycle=Peck, peck_increment=...)  [the bore carries its own extent, measured down from its rim]
# extent=11.0 reaches the drill TIP; the full-diameter depth is 8.0
# match the drill's point angle (~118.072 deg) to reproduce the bottom exactly
feature F8_Hole CylinderBore(dia=10.0, extent=11.0, x=50.0, y=20.0)

# F9: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; flat floor F12 -- a milled bore (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F9_Bore, stepover=...)  [stepover is the ring spacing up the wall]
# a flat floor is milled, not drilled -- a twist drill leaves a conical point, so no drill run is suggested
feature F9_Bore CylinderBore(dia=16.0, extent=6.0, x=80.0, y=20.0)

# F10: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; bottom is not a flat floor or drill point -- proposed wall-only as a milled bore (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F10_Bore, stepover=...)  [stepover is the ring spacing up the wall]
# wall-only proposal: the bottom face is not reproducible by drill or a flat-floor bore (see its own report entry)
feature F10_Bore CylinderBore(dia=10.0, extent=7.0, x=20.0, y=60.0)
